From: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] map-agent: emit valid JSON for the backhaul in agent status

`ubus call map.agent status` opens "backhaul" as a table and then places an
unkeyed table inside it:

	d = blobmsg_open_table(&bb, "backhaul");
	if (re->has_bsta && re->bk.cfg) {
		ttt = blobmsg_open_table(&bb, "");

An unkeyed member is array syntax, so the rendered document is

	"backhaul": {
		{
			"name": "wlan2",

which is not JSON. Parsers do not skip the malformed member - they reject
the whole document:

	jsonfilter: Failed to parse JSON data: quoted object property name expected
	python:     Expecting property name enclosed in double quotes: line 57 column 5

So nothing on the node can parse the agent's own status output, on every
node that has a backhaul STA. The failure is silent in the worst way: a
caller reading a count out of it gets 0 rather than an error, which reads
as "healthy node with nothing configured".

The surrounding code already treats this as a list - the line above closes
the previous member with blobmsg_close_array(), and the sibling radio
status uses blobmsg_open_array(&bb, "backhauls") for the same shape. Open
it as an array so the unkeyed table becomes a legitimate element.

Keys and their indentation are unchanged, so line-based readers - which is
everything that works today, by necessity - are unaffected.

Found while writing mld-report-check, which needs to count the affiliated
APs the agent reports. Measured on bpi-8g and bpi-x8, 2026-07-22.

Signed-off-by: Petr Wozniak <petr.wozniak@gmail.com>
---
--- a/src/agent.c	2026-07-22 06:36:36.765439704 +0200
+++ b/src/agent.c	2026-07-22 06:36:36.781001108 +0200
@@ -5955,7 +5955,7 @@
 			blobmsg_close_table(&bb, tt);
 		}
 		blobmsg_close_array(&bb, d);
-		d = blobmsg_open_table(&bb, "backhaul");
+		d = blobmsg_open_array(&bb, "backhaul");
 		if (re->has_bsta && re->bk.cfg) {
 			struct netif_bk *bk = &re->bk;
 			void *ttt;
@@ -5990,7 +5990,7 @@
 			blobmsg_close_table(&bb, b);
 			blobmsg_close_table(&bb, ttt);
 		}
-		blobmsg_close_table(&bb, d);
+		blobmsg_close_array(&bb, d);
 		blobmsg_close_table(&bb, t);
 	}
 	blobmsg_close_array(&bb, a);
